slices.what:
graph/jevrun.js is an incremental reducer over `log --json` lines.
The graph:
- It joins the jev_graph 'jev-page next=' ToolResults into the exact graph text the run used (interp.rn:751-800) and reads states, floor and margin (state meta, then meta.jev.defaults) and the entail threshold from it.
- If no pages were journaled, it takes the installed graph passed in, labelled 'drawn from the installed graph; may differ from the one this run used'.
Output:
- meta {graph, start, goal}; status, plus unresumable {step, reason}; active state, visited states, path
- steps[], each with:
  - n, state, ts_ms and duration_ms
  - page {url, title, heading, chars}
  - arrival {equals {heading, goal, hit}; entail {score, threshold, hit} | error}
  - jev {context_cut (first 192 bytes, UTF-8 safe), options_cut [32-byte cuts], collisions [[i, j]]}
  - menu {options [{label, p}], source chooser|rule|single, top1, top2, floor, margin, floorOk, marginOk}
  - park {call_id, prompt, answer?, invalid?}
  - pick {label, index, how}
  - action {tool, input, result | error}
- budgets {decisions, actions, escalations: used/cap; host steps used/200}
- spend[]
Unknown record kinds are ignored.
